    {
      "topLeftX": 65,
      "topLeftY": 518,
      "bottomRightX": 726,
      "bottomRightY": 555,
      "content": "ITU-R BT.709 provides a definition of the Y', Cb and Cr based on (1). It defines signal range identical to BT.601, as expressed in (9).",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 65,
      "topLeftY": 562,
      "bottomRightX": 610,
      "bottomRightY": 581,
      "content": "But its luma equation is based on (2). Hence its 2 color difference signals are given by:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 587,
      "bottomRightX": 702,
      "bottomRightY": 606,
      "content": "$$\\mathrm{E}'_{\\mathrm{B}} - \\mathrm{E}'_{\\mathrm{Y}} \\quad \\text{is in the range } [-0.9278, +0.9278] \\tag{12}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 113,
      "topLeftY": 612,
      "bottomRightX": 419,
      "bottomRightY": 632,
      "content": "$$\\mathrm{E}'_{\\mathrm{R}} - \\mathrm{E}'_{\\mathrm{Y}} \\quad \\text{is in the range } [-0.7874, +0.7874]$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 66,
      "topLeftY": 665,
      "bottomRightX": 389,
      "bottomRightY": 683,
      "content": "After normalization to occupy the [-0.5, 0.5] range:",
